{"title":"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 45","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_45&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A wheel with a rubber tire has an outside diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> in. When the radius has been decreased a quarter of an inch, the number of revolutions in one mile will:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54c51a31456ac73d9539cd190b44a11665492b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\text{be increased about }2\\% \\qquad \\\\ \\text{(B)}\\ \\text{be increased about }1\\%  \\\\ \\text{(C)}\\ \\text{be increased about }20\\%\\qquad \\\\ \\text{(D)}\\ \\text{be increased about }\\frac{1}{2}\\%\\qquad \\\\ \\text{(E)}\\ \\text{remain the same}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"116\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_45&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> be the initial radius of the wheel and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> be the decreased radius.\n</p><p>Since the initial outside diameter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/4/b7465f459e73f476dd4567b1fcc0fb5d45bb36da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\text{ in.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, the initial radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b1f20ebe4a696a5c0f85facac949a0a715aa2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 = 12.5\\text{ in.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>When the radius is decreased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3abf56c3efcd72552af67b45de8e5ad7baef9c5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}\\text{ in.} = 0.25\\text{ in.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"38\" />, the new radius is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d31e773f435015afe8f9c13567897a8ca98f1d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r_2 = 12.5 - 0.25 = 12.25\\text{ in.}\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>The number of revolutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> needed to cover a fixed distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> (such as one mile) is inversely proportional to the circumference of the wheel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69a09c64e5a8fc8643432d6afd67f1a17210cf6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 2\\pi r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce407e03ea7c061aa689bdd7f77ffa4dc80df7d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = \\frac{D}{2\\pi r}\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/535f2647ce093bccd2a78a1174e6714a1d035a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e715db9bdeefe6c4f6b079451b994061a92e40f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> be the initial and new number of revolutions, respectively. The ratio of the new number of revolutions to the initial number is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3d8e13fc6069cc710ab7103d1b809c9bd675c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{N_2}{N_1} = \\frac{r_1}{r_2} = \\frac{12.5}{12.25} = \\frac{1250}{1225} = \\frac{50}{49}\\]\" width=\"247\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>The relative increase in the number of revolutions is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57d803e74c97448d9d929bb668c68ec6c17567ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{N_2 - N_1}{N_1} = \\frac{N_2}{N_1} - 1 = \\frac{50}{49} - 1 = \\frac{1}{49} \\approx 0.0204 = 2.04\\%\\]\" width=\"419\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the number of revolutions will be increased by about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b04a3bd51b4c6a454c3aae545a1dbc6a5bff05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" />, which corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_45&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME\" title=\"1956 AHSME\">1956 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1956 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1956\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_44\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 44\">Problem 44</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_46\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 46\">Problem 46</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems